   "definition_quote": "I study the simplest setting with $K$ arms and a subgaussian noise model. In each time step $t$ the learner chooses an action $I_t \\in \\set{1,\\ldots,K}$ and receives a reward $\\mu_{I_t} + \\eta_t$ where $\\mu_i$ is the unknown expected reward of arm $i$ and the noise term $\\eta_t$ is sampled from some $1$-subgaussian distribution that may depend on $I_t$."
